From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LECH OS <dev@lech-os.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Leave out the eSIM apps of Google

LECH OS has no eSIM support for now. On the Pixel 9 the eSIM apps of
Google (EuiccGoogle, EuiccSupportPixel) contacted lpa.live.esimdiscovery.com
(Google) and lpa.ds.gsma.com at every start, and the system enabled them
again after `pm disable-user`. The vendor module leaves them out; the
physical SIM is not affected. eSIM can come back later as an explicit
choice.
---
 config/device/common/apk.yml | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/config/device/common/apk.yml b/config/device/common/apk.yml
index a8d08477..56066e2b 100644
--- a/config/device/common/apk.yml
+++ b/config/device/common/apk.yml
@@ -838,6 +838,12 @@ package_exclusions:
   - com.verizon.mips.services
   - com.verizon.services
   - com.vzw.apnlib
+  # LECH OS: no eSIM support for now - the eSIM apps of Google contacted lpa.live.esimdiscovery.com (Google) and
+  # lpa.ds.gsma.com at every start and were enabled again after `pm disable-user` (network audit, 7. 11. 2026).
+  - com.google.android.euicc
+  - com.google.android.euiccoverlay
+  - com.google.euiccpixel
+  - com.google.euiccpixel.permissions
 
 # GrapheneOS APK path to stock OS package
 apk_map:
-- 
2.43.0

